{"schema_version":"1.7.5","id":"OESA-2026-3184","published":"2026-07-24T03:31:40Z","modified":"2026-07-24T03:45:17.124697922Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-26018"],"summary":"coredns security update","details":"CoreDNS is a fast and flexible DNS server. The key word here is flexible: with CoreDNS you are able to do what you want with your DNS data by utilizing plugins.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nCoreDNS is a DNS server that chains plugins. Prior to version 1.14.2, a denial of service vulnerability exists in CoreDNS&apos;s loop detection plugin that allows an attacker to crash the DNS server by sending specially crafted DNS queries. The vulnerability stems from the use of a predictable pseudo-random number generator (PRNG) for generating a secret query name, combined with a fatal error handler that terminates the entire process. This issue has been patched in version 1.14.2.(CVE-2026-26018)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"coredns","ecosystem":"openEuler:24.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/coredns&distro=openEuler-24.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.7.0-1.7.oe2403sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["coredns-1.7.0-1.7.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm","coredns-help-1.7.0-1.7.oe2403sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["coredns-1.7.0-1.7.oe2403sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["coredns-1.7.0-1.7.oe2403sp4.x86_64.rpm","coredns-help-1.7.0-1.7.oe2403sp4.x86_64.rpm"]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://repo.openeuler.org/security/data/osv/OESA-2026-3184.json"}},{"package":{"name":"coredns","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/coredns&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.7.0-1.5.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["coredns-1.7.0-1.5.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","coredns-help-1.7.0-1.5.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm"],"src":["coredns-1.7.0-1.5.oe2003sp4.src.rpm"],"x86_64":["coredns-1.7.0-1.5.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm","coredns-help-1.7.0-1.5.oe2003sp4.x86_64.rpm"]}